A lost Daft Punk mix from 1997 has been rediscovered, restored and made available to listen to – check it out below.

Leeds-based DJ Ralph Lawson was sent the hour-long mix by the French electronic duo in February 1997, shortly after the release of their debut album ‘ Homework ’, to play on his Kiss 105 FM radio show Trans Europe Express .

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

Lawson, a founding resident DJ at Leeds’ Back To Basics club night, had befriended Thomas Bangalter and Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo after opening for them at a show that year, where drum’n’bass pioneer Goldie topped the bill.

Having played the mix on his radio show, Lawson put the digital audio tape (DAT) into storage, where it remained until he came across it again in 2024. However, it had developed mould over the intervening decades and tore when he attempted to play it.

He enlisted the help of Bristol-based audio preservation specialists Greatbear, who spent several weeks painstakingly repairing and cleaning the tape.

“It’s nice to make people happy through this kind of restoration work,” said Greatbear’s Adrian Finn, who admitted to dancing while listening back to the recording. “I thought it was good and glad it played back with hardly any errors.”

